('wikiloc', '210661990', 'https://www.wikiloc.com/hiking-trails/fuerte-de-rostrogordo-from-the-port-melilla-210661990', 'Fuerte de Rostrogordo - Melilla', '{"en":"Long loop from Ferry Terminal","ca":"Circular llarga des de la Terminal de Ferry","es":"Circular larga desde la Terminal de Ferry"}'::jsonb, 'Fuerte de Rostrogordo - Melilla Hiking trail in Melilla, Melilla (España). Download its GPS track and follow the itinerary on a map. A hike to the highest point in Melilla. 
 
Melilla, in addition to Ceuta, is one of the two autonomous cities of Spain, both exclaves in North Africa, surrounded by Morocco on the southern shores of the Alboran Sea in the westernmost part of the Mediterranen Sea. The area of Melilla is approx. 12 km² and its population approx. 86,000. 
 
This visit was made by ferry t/r from Motril, an overnight journey of 5 hours, with retour in the afternoon on the arrival day. Such one can start the trail early in the morning and still have time to explore the city centre, and have some relaxing time before departure back to Motril. 
 
The highest point of Melilla standing at 137 masl. is located approx. 250 meters west of Fuerte de Rostrogordo only a few meters from the Moroccan border. The fort, completed in 1890, is a Site of Cultural Interest, one of the outer forts in the northern part of Melilla. 
 
The trail from outside the ferry terminal passes through: 
 
- Baluarte de San José 0.5 km 
- Fuerte de Victoria Chica 1.0 km 
- Fuerte Rostrogordo 4.9 km 
- Miarador del Barranco Queradero 5.8 km 
- Melilla High Point 6.6 km 
- Cerro de las Tres Coronas 7.3 km 
- Embalse de las Adelfas 8.1 km 
- Iglesias del Sagrado Corazon de Jesus 11 km 
- Parque Hernandez 11.2 km 
- Plaza de España 11.5 km 
- The MELILLA letters 11.9 km 
 
After the hiking-part of the visit (I ended recording this loop-trail when I arrived back at the ferry terminal), I spend some time at the walled citadel "Melilla La Vieja", situated close to the terminal. A visit to the citadel is highly recommended.', '{"en":"This easy 12.5 km loop starts near the Melilla ferry terminal and leads to the highest point of Melilla (137m), located west of Fuerte de Rostrogordo and close to the Moroccan border. The route passes several historical forts, including Baluarte de San José and Fuerte de Victoria Chica, before reaching Fuerte Rostrogordo, completed in 1890.\n\nThe trail continues to the Mirador del Barranco Queradero and Cerro de las Tres Coronas, offering a mix of urban and natural landscapes. It concludes by passing the Embalse de las Adelfas and returning through the city center, visiting landmarks like the Iglesias del Sagrado Corazon de Jesus and Plaza de España.","ca":"Aquesta ruta circular fàcil de 12,5 km comença prop de la terminal de ferri de Melilla i porta al punt més alt de Melilla (137m), situat a l''oest del Fuerte de Rostrogordo i prop de la frontera marroquina. La ruta passa per diverses fortificacions històriques, incloent el Baluarte de San José i el Fuerte de Victoria Chica, abans d''arribar al Fuerte Rostrogordo, completat el 1890.\n\nEl camí continua cap al Mirador del Barranco Queradero i el Cerro de las Tres Coronas, oferint una barreja de paisatges urbans i naturals. Conclou passant per l''Embalse de las Adelfas i tornant pel centre de la ciutat, visitant llocs d''interès com les Iglesias del Sagrado Corazon de Jesus i la Plaza de España.","es":"Esta ruta circular fácil de 12,5 km comienza cerca de la terminal de ferry de Melilla y lleva al punto más alto de Melilla (137m), situado al oeste del Fuerte de Rostrogordo y cerca de la frontera marroquí. La ruta pasa por varias fortificaciones históricas, incluyendo el Baluarte de San José y el Fuerte de Victoria Chica, antes de llegar al Fuerte Rostrogordo, completado en 1890.\n\nEl sendero continúa hacia el Mirador del Barranco Queradero y el Cerro de las Tres Coronas, ofreciendo una mezcla de paisajes urbanos y naturales. Concluye pasando por el Embalse de las Adelfas y regresando por el centro de la ciudad, visitando lugares de interés como las Iglesias del Sagrado Corazon de Jesus y la Plaza de España."}'::jsonb, 'Senderista Noruego', 12505, 238, 238, 141, 1, 'easy', 'loop', 10500, 14340, 2192, '2025-04-24', '2025-03', '[{"lat":35.292258,"lng":-2.933148,"ele":4.1},{"lat":35.292283,"lng":-2.933194,"ele":4.2},{"lat":35.292299,"lng":-2.933249,"ele":4.3},{"lat":35.292316,"lng":-2.933301,"ele":4.3},{"lat":35.29233,"lng":-2.933363,"ele":4.3},{"lat":35.292342,"lng":-2.933425,"ele":4.1},{"lat":35.292348,"lng":-2.933483,"ele":4},{"lat":35.29237,"lng":-2.933541,"ele":3.7},{"lat":35.292406,"lng":-2.933595,"ele":3.4},{"lat":35.292438,"lng":-2.933645,"ele":3.1},{"lat":35.292466,"lng":-2.933699,"ele":2.8},{"lat":35.292479,"lng":-2.933752,"ele":2.5},{"lat":35.292509,"lng":-2.933809,"ele":2.6},{"lat":35.292537,"lng":-2.933864,"ele":3.2},{"lat":35.292569,"lng":-2.933905,"ele":3.8},{"lat":35.292617,"lng":-2.933947,"ele":4.7},{"lat":35.292663,"lng":-2.933977,"ele":5.5},{"lat":35.292714,"lng":-2.933966,"ele":7},{"lat":35.292767,"lng":-2.933977,"ele":8.1},{"lat":35.29282,"lng":-2.934001,"ele":9.3},{"lat":35.292852,"lng":-2.934044,"ele":9.4},{"lat":35.292884,"lng":-2.934092,"ele":9.3},{"lat":35.29292,"lng":-2.934145,"ele":9.1},{"lat":35.292946,"lng":-2.934191,"ele":8.9},{"lat":35.292976,"lng":-2.934241,"ele":8.8},{"lat":35.293001,"lng":-2.934292,"ele":8.4},{"lat":35.293021,"lng":-2.934356,"ele":7.5},{"lat":35.293044,"lng":-2.934408,"ele":6.7},{"lat":35.29307,"lng":-2.934463,"ele":6.1},{"lat":35.293098,"lng":-2.934507,"ele":6.3},{"lat":35.293117,"lng":-2.93456,"ele":6.3},{"lat":35.293134,"lng":-2.934627,"ele":6.1},{"lat":35.293133,"lng":-2.934682,"ele":5.8},{"lat":35.293136,"lng":-2.93474,"ele":5.7},{"lat":35.293123,"lng":-2.934793,"el