('wikiloc', '212461229', 'https://www.wikiloc.com/hiking-trails/monte-anyera-and-monte-hacho-ceuta-212461229', 'Monte Ányera and Monte Hacho - Ceuta', '{"en":"Long loop including Monte Hacho","ca":"Circular llarga incloent Monte Hacho","es":"Circular larga incluyendo Monte Hacho"}'::jsonb, 'Monte Ányera and Monte Hacho - Ceuta Hiking trail in Ceuta, Ceuta (España). Download its GPS track and follow the itinerary on a map. A long hike to the highest points west and east in Ceuta. 
 
Ceuta, in addition to Melilla, is one of the two autonomous cities of Spain, both exclaves in North-Africa, surrounded by Morocco. It lies along the boundary between the Mediterranean Sea and the Atlantic Ocean. The area of Ceuta is approx. 18.5 km² and its population approx. 83,300. 
 
The visit was made by speed-ferry t/r from Algeciras, a convenient trip of one hour, with retour in the afternoon on the arrival day. When starting the hike early in the morning one will have sufficient time for this trail before departure back to Algeciras. If the trail becomes too exhausting one can book an overnight stay and split it over two-days. I rate it as moderate only due to its length. There are one steep part up to Fuerte Ányera and one to Monte Hacho to overcome. Technically it''s easy. 
 
First part (from ferry port and back ) 17.2 km - 678 m elevation gain. 
The highest point west in Ceuta (and overall) at 344 masl., is located at Monte Ányera with its Torre de Ányera, 300 meters from the Moroccan border. The tower-fortress was was completed in 1864. It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. 
 
Second part (from ferry port and back) -11.1 km - 200 m elevation gain 
The highest point east in Ceuta at 154 masl., is located at Monte Hacho with its Fortaleza de Hacho (some sources says it stands at 190 masl.). The views from the fortress over the city is spectacular and its walls can be seen from virtually any point in the city and from the sea. 
 
The two parts (hiked as one continous trail) totals 28.3 km, with a total elevation gain of 878 meter, and passes through: 
 
- Mirador Isabel II (4.4 km) 
- Fuerte de Isabel II (5.3 km) 
- Monte Ányera (8.1 km) 
- Torre de Aranguren (9.1 km) 
- Mirador de Beliunes (9.5 km) 
- Monte Tortuga (12.0 km) 
- Embalse del Renegado (13.8 km) 
- Playa Benitez (15.3 km) 
- Ferry Port 
- The Pillars of Hércules (18.8 km) 
- Casa de los Dragones (19.2 km) 
- Baños Árabes (20.1 km) 
- Parque de San Amaro (21.3 km) 
- Mirador San Antonio (22.6 km) 
- Monte Hacho (23.4 km) 
- Playa La Ribera (26.7 km) 
- Murallas Reales (27.1 km) 
- Estacion de Ferrocarill (27.9 km)', '{"en":"This long, moderate 28.3 km loop is a demanding day hike to the highest points of Ceuta, Monte Anyera (344m) and Monte Hacho (154m). Starting from the ferry port, the first part of the route leads to Monte Anyera, featuring a steep ascent to Fuerte Anyera, a UNESCO World Heritage site near the Moroccan border.\n\nThe second part of the loop returns to the ferry port before heading east to Monte Hacho, which also involves a steep climb to its fortress. While technically easy, the overall length and significant elevation gain make this a challenging route suitable for experienced hikers.","ca":"Aquesta ruta circular llarga i moderada de 28,3 km és una excursió d''un dia exigent als punts més alts de Ceuta, el Monte Anyera (344m) i el Monte Hacho (154m). Començant des del port del ferri, la primera part de la ruta condueix al Monte Anyera, amb una pujada pronunciada fins al Fuerte Anyera, un lloc Patrimoni de la Humanitat de la UNESCO prop de la frontera marroquina.\n\nLa segona part del circuit torna al port del ferri abans de dirigir-se a l''est cap al Monte Hacho, que també implica una pujada pronunciada fins a la seva fortalesa. Tot i ser tècnicament fàcil, la longitud total i el considerable desnivell fan d''aquesta una ruta desafiant apta per a excursionistes experimentats.","es":"Esta ruta circular larga y moderada de 28,3 km es una caminata de un día exigente a los puntos más altos de Ceuta, el Monte Anyera (344m) y el Monte Hacho (154m). Comenzando desde el puerto del ferry, la primera parte de la ruta conduce al Monte Anyera, con un ascenso empinado hasta el Fuerte Anyera, un sitio Patrimonio de la Humanidad de la UNESCO cerca de la frontera marroquí.\n\nLa segunda parte del circuito regresa al puerto del ferry antes de dirigirse al este hacia el Monte Hacho, que también implica una subida empinada hasta su fortaleza. Aunque técnicamente fácil, la longitud total y el considerable desnivel hacen de esta una ruta desafiante apta para excursionistas experimentados."}'::jsonb, 'Senderista Noruego', 28308, 878, 878, 345, 1, 'moderate', 'loop', 22260, 26940, 4959, '2025-05-05', '2025-04', '[{"lat":35.893196,"lng":-5.321058,"ele":2.9},{"lat":35.893145,"lng":-5.321085,"ele":2.9},{"lat":35.893106,"lng":-5.321121,"ele":3},{"lat":35.893068,"lng":-5.321166,"ele":3},{"lat":35.893046,"lng":-5.321217,"ele":3},{"lat":35.892997,"lng":-5.321254,"ele":3.1},{"lat":35.892979,"lng":-5.321317,"ele":3.2},{"lat":35.892933,"lng":-5.32132,"ele":3.3},{"lat":35.892891,"lng":-5.321358,"ele":3.5},{"lat":35.892885,"lng":-5.321414,"ele":3.7},{"lat":35.8929,"lng":-5.321484,"ele":3.8},{"lat":35.892915,"lng":-5.32154,"ele":3.8},{"lat":35.892955,"lng":-5.321591,"ele":3.6},{"lat":35.892986,"lng":-5.321633,"ele":3.5},{"lat":35.893024,"lng":-5.321685,"ele":3.2},{"lat":35.893058,"lng":-5.321736,"ele":3},{"lat":35.893086,"lng":-5.321783,"ele":2.9},{"lat":35.893118,"lng":-5.32183,"ele":2.8},{"lat":35.893159,"lng":-5.321874,"ele":2.6},{"lat":35.893193,"lng":-5.321928,"ele":2.5},{"lat":35.89323,"lng":-5.321982,"ele":2.4},{"lat":35.893266,"lng":-5.322026,"ele":2.2},{"lat":35.893295,"lng":-5.322072,"ele":2.1},{"lat":35.893332,"lng":-5.322116,"ele":2},{"lat":35.893361,"lng":-5.322172,"ele":1.9},{"lat":35.893396,"lng":-5.322219,"ele":1.8},{"lat":35.893434,"lng":-5.322266,"ele":1.6},{"lat":35.893461,"lng":-5.322312,"ele":1.5},{"lat":35.893501,"lng":-5.322361,"ele":1.4},{"lat":35.893542,"lng":-5.322409,"ele":1.2},{"lat":35.893572,"lng":-5.322454,"ele":1.1},{"lat":35.893604,"lng":-5.322495,"ele":1},{"lat":35.893634,"lng":-5.322539,"ele":1.2},{"lat":35.893674,"lng":-5.322589,"ele":1.6},{"lat":35.893714,"lng":-5.322616,"ele":1.9},{"lat":35.893754,"lng":-5.322657,"ele":2.4},{"lat":35.893802,"lng":-5.322699,"ele":2.9},{"lat":35.893841,"lng":-5.322749,"ele":3.5},{"lat":35.893874,"lng":-5.322803,"ele":4},{"lat":35.893899,"lng":-5.322862,"ele":4.3},{"lat":35.893912,"lng":-5.32293,"ele":4.5},{"lat":35.893941,"lng":-5.32299,"ele":4.8}